From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: IamMaxim <g.maxim.stepanoff@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 15 Jun 2026 14:49:51 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Make activate_project_group host-aware for remote project
 tabs

MultiWorkspace::activate_project_group unconditionally fell back to
find_or_create_local_workspace when a project group was not already
retained, ignoring key.host(). For remote groups (SSH/WSL/Docker) this
opened the remote paths as a bogus local workspace -- triggered after
restart, when restored groups have last_active_workspace: None.

Mirror the sidebar's open_workspace_for_group: for local groups keep the
existing local path; for remote groups route through the host-aware
find_or_create_workspace so the host is reconnected. Since the workspace
crate cannot depend on remote_connection (cycle), the modal-based
connector is injected by the app layer via set_remote_connector, using a
RemoteConnector exposed from the sidebar crate.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
